{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NzVXU5b7TKbfounW71rPUm","type":"tool_result","content":"### 2.5 L3 — the MOSP forms\n\nLet the instance have customers `C` (`|C| = n`) and patterns\n`S_1, …, S_m ⊆ C`; its MOSP graph `mospGraph` (`MOSPGraph.lean`;\n`coverGraph` in `CliqueCoverMoment.lean`) joins two distinct customers\niff some pattern contains both, and `mospValue = pw(mospGraph) + 1`\n(`MOSPGraph.lean`, both directions). With `k = mospValue − 1 < n`:\n\n**Lemma L3.** (a) For disjoint `A, R ⊆ C`, `(A, R)` is an empty pair of\n`mospGraph` iff no pattern meets both `A` and `R`\n(`isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff`). (b) L1, L1′ and L2 hold for `mospGraph`\nwith `S` a set of `k` customers; in particular every instance with\n`mospValue ≤ k + 1` has `k` customers whose removal leaves customer\nclasses of sizes `t` and `N − t` such that no pattern meets both classes.\n(c) In a closed pair `(A*, R*)` of `mospGraph`, a customer `c` lies in\n`S* = N(A*) ∩ N(R*)` iff `c ∉ A* ∪ R*`, some pattern contains `c` and a\ncustomer of `A*`, and some pattern contains `c` and a customer of `R*`.\n\n*Proof.* (a) is the cited lemma. (b) is L1, L1′, L2 applied to the graph\n`mospGraph`, with `k ≥ pw` given by the equality theorem. (c) `c ∈ N(X)`\nfor `mospGraph` means `c ∉ X` and `c` is adjacent to some `x ∈ X`, i.e.\nsome pattern contains both `c` and `x`; apply L2 (iv). ∎\n\nThe check of §2.4 runs L1, L1′, L2 on the MOSP graphs of 2,000 random\ncovers and tests (a) and (c) directly against the matrix.\n\n### 2.6 Lean-ready statements for item 10\n-----\n\"\"\"loop0011 item 02: the deterministic lemmas of the separator first moment\n(`learning.separator_moment`, `reports/separator_moment.md` §2).\n\nL1  a graph of pathwidth `k < n` has an exact-size empty pair (`|A| = ⌈(n − k)/2⌉`,\n    `|R| = ⌊(n − k)/2⌋`);\nL1′ equivalently a `k`-set `S` in `E_bip`; `E_bip ⊆ E_relax`, strictly;\nL2  the alternating closure of any empty pair is monotone, stops after one\n    round, and lands on a closed pair `S* = N(A*) ∩ N(R*)` of the forced sizes;\nL3  on the MOSP graph a pair is empty iff no pattern meets both sides.\n\nEvery labelled graph on ≤ 6 vertices is enumerated here; the full check (every\ngraph to 9 vertices, 20,000 random at 10–12, 2,000 covers) is\n`reports/scratch/separator_moment/02_lemmas/check.py`.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport math\nimport random\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\nimport networkx as nx\nimport numpy as np\nimport pytest\n\nfrom benchmarks.generator import generate_structured_instance\nfrom fixed_parameter_algorithm.pathwidth import compute_pathwidth\nfrom learning.first_moment import vertex_separation_brute\nfrom learning.separator_moment import (\n    close_pair, closed_pairs, closure_sequence, count_exact_pairs, count_separators,\n    exact_pairs, forced_sizes, is_closed_pair, is_empty_pair, mosp_masks, open_nbhd,\n    pattern_meets_both, popcount, separator_events, shares_pattern, vertex_separation,\n)\n\n\ndef all_labelled_graphs(n):\n    pairs = list(combinations(range(n), 2))\n    for mask in range(1 << len(pairs)):\n        adj = [0] * n\n        for i, (u, v) in enumerate(pairs):\n            if mask >> i & 1:\n                adj[u] |= 1 << v\n                adj[v] |= 1 << u\n        yield adj\n\n\ndef random_graph(n, p, seed):\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    adj = [0] * n\n    for u, v in combinations(range(n), 2):\n        if rng.random() < p:\n            adj[u] |= 1 << v\n            adj[v] |= 1 << u\n    return adj\n\n\ndef test_vertex_separation_agrees_with_the_two_other_implementations():\n    for n in range(1, 6):\n        for adj in all_labelled_graphs(n):\n            G = nx.Graph()\n            G.add_nodes_from(range(n))\n47","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d18e1e5c-be10-4026-a9cc-cded248cca2c","uuid":"b3bd6e9c-870c-40a3-8cc3-8bb50e2a460c","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:02:09.834Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 2.5 