{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgckFMZ95dzZa5mJqk2wh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 07 is complete and the gate passed. Six items remain unchecked, so no LOOP_COMPLETE line is added.\n\n**What was done.** Item 07, the MOSP version of the separator first moment on random clique covers, is finished. Deliverables: `reports/separator_moment.md` §7, the cover functions in `learning/separator_moment.py`, four new tests, and the scratch outputs under `reports/scratch/separator_moment/07_cover/`.\n\n**Findings.**\n- **Kill criterion met.** The closed-pair count lifts the constant by +0.0111 at (6, 1) and +0.0110 at (4, 1), below the 0.02 line at both named cells. The route is closed for the headline constants on covers, as it was on G(n, c/n).\n- **Where the count is worth most.** The gain is a sparse-side one, largest at few and large patterns: +0.021 at (8, ½), above the line, and +0.018 to +0.020 at (6, ½) and (10, ½). Recorded as a separate finding outside the kill's scope.\n- **The flips** add 0.001 to 0.006 in β at μ ≥ 1, up to +0.017 at (4, ½). The supremum sits at one side with no isolated customer in every cell, the mechanism item 09 was told to expect.\n- **Half-giant line.** θ = ½ at excess 0.60 to 0.82 for μ from ⅛ to 2, between the giant-onset line and the pair threshold, as the plan predicted. The threshold proposition is proved from L3 and pattern thinning, conditional on a large-deviation hypothesis that no held paper states for random intersection graphs. The ensemble check cannot confirm the line because the generators repair and reject disconnected instances.\n- **Floors on the 200 Chu & Stuckey instances.** Zero violations at the 0.01 threshold for all four counts. The closed floor beats the exact-size pair floor on 97 instances and loses on none, by 0.4 to 1.6 stacks at 125×125. The flip floor beats it on 35, the d = 2 classes.\n- **The cancellation-free bound costs nothing.** The negative-association bound sits a constant 0.2 nats above the exact alternating sum, so the exact closed-pair rate is the independent-sites one to the fit's accuracy.\n\n**Corrections to the item** are in §7.7: the inclusion–exclusion collapses to (s+1)² integer terms with no mpmath, the item's isolated-customer generating function is the wrong conditional law, and two root-finding defects in the first grid run were fixed and the cheap columns recomputed.\n\n**Compute.** About 2.0 core-hours against 1 budgeted; the overrun is in the flip roots on the pooled-size cells. Gate: PASS, with 1,730 tests passed and zero sorry or axiom.\n\n**Next.** Item 08 can take the closed-pair formula, the negative-association corollary, the cover flip count and the conditional threshold proposition verbatim from §7; item 12 should carry Edwards & McDermid on the cover grid and the half-giant line as the proposed figure addition."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":732,"cache_read_input_tokens":347547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":732,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":773,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d18e1e5c-be10-4026-a9cc-cded248cca2c","uuid":"32a259e6-fccc-4b80-a7e4-299a2ee7aec4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:18:01.720Z","request_id":"req_011CgckFM8qaEZPRh9LAo2eB"}
